ix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of ${I}_{3}$ and subtracting the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555791 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555791 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110463" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555791 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555791 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555791 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3a8b7714-d243-5a18-865d-0e2cf918670b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555791 #edb/ref 1074 "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the third row of ${I}_{3}$ and adding $7$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1}$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555797 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555797 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110476" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555797 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555797 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the elementary row operation \n${R}_{3}:=\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555797 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "44c4828d-5d0a-5c06-aad5-ea02f733cf44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555797 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555812 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555812 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110470" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555812 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555812 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555812 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5e29c468-7ba6-5997-83d8-49458f8bde8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555812 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555834 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555834 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75162" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555834 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555834 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:=-8{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555834 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "941b6a8e-c424-5e02-9c9b-4d19cc52c2d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555834 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{1}:=-8{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
